427	<section id="findings">
428	  <div class="sec-head reveal"><span class="sec-no">05</span><h2>Findings</h2></div>
429	  <h3>1 · Most of it is medium-consistent — gains and losses alike</h3>
430	  <p>Of 456 genes whose essentiality differs between organoids and conventional cultures,
431	  <b>86% of gains and 84% of losses meet our medium-consistency criteria</b> (same-direction effect, at least half as large, in flat-grown cells fed organoid medium)
432	  (75–82% under conservative robust statistics). The strongest class is cholesterol/sterol manufacture
433	  (SQLE, MSMO1), followed by fatty-acid and heme synthesis — exactly the pathways a serum-free,
434	  lipid-poor diet would stress. Gene-expression data show the mirror image (cholesterol genes switched
435	  <i>on</i> in organoid medium, the classic starvation response), and in independent screens using
436	  blood-like medium, the flagship gene SQLE moves the <i>opposite</i> way.</p>
437	  <figure class="figwrap reveal"><img src="assets/fig1.png" alt="Attribution scatter plots">
438	  <figcaption><b>Figure 1.</b> Left: flat-grown, same-medium effect vs organoid effect — points hug the diagonal.
439	  Right: the shape-only contrast (dome vs flat within organoid medium) — a shapeless cloud near zero.</figcaption></figure>
440	
441	  <h3>2 · Auditing the published target lists</h3>
442	  <p>Against the Broad catalogue&rsquo;s own published hits: 47% are medium-consistent overall, and 87% of those
443	  that replicate under lineage adjustment. Against Sanger&rsquo;s &ldquo;organoid-specific core fitness&rdquo;
444	  headline-18: 8 of 16 replicate here, 5 are medium-consistent — four of them the SREBP/sterol axis
445	  (MVD, IDI1, MBTPS1, MBTPS2) — and 3 remain unresolved (SCAP, DDX3X, ITGB1), making them the more
446	  credible follow-up candidates. Sanger&rsquo;s own calls are prevalent in their assay (median depletion
447	  in 70–80% of organoids); the issue is attribution, not call quality.</p>
448	  <figure class="figwrap reveal"><img src="assets/fig3.png" alt="Flag composition of published hit lists">
449	  <figcaption><b>Figure 3.</b> Composition of the published hit lists under our flags. Grey = does not reproduce
450	  as a hit under lineage adjustment (attribution unestablished — not evidence of real biology).</figcaption></figure>

